<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tages</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tages was a figure of Etruscan religion, a child with the wisdom of an old man who, according to legend, sprang from a ploughed furrow near Tarquinii. He was said to have revealed the Etruscan discipline of divination, including the reading of entrails by haruspices, to the leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>. Roman writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> recorded the tale, and books of ritual attributed to him formed part of the Etrusca disciplina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tages.jpg" alt="Tages" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarquinia_-_Ara_della_Regina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
